1. Start with the initial number of carrots Maria picked: 48 carrots. 2. Subtract the number of carrots she threw out: 48 - 11 = 37 carrots. 3. Add the number of carrots she picked the next day: 37 + 15 = 52 carrots. 
Therefore, Maria would have 52 carrots total.
\boxed{52}

